-Add a regression test:I can't run the build/test here — installing dependencies is blocked by the sandbox policy and `node_modules` isn't present, so the typecheck and mocha runs are unverified.

Summary of the fix:

**Cause** — src/index.ts:86 called `handlers.splice(handlers.indexOf(handler), 1)`. When `handler` was never registered, `indexOf` returns -1, and `splice(-1, 1)` removes the **last** element of the array — a completely different handler.

**Fix** — only splice when the handler is actually found:

```ts
const index = handlers.indexOf(handler);
if (index > -1) {
    handlers.splice(index, 1);
}
```

